== Increasing drop chances ==
Drops from killing a mob that is not a [[Slayer|Slayer Boss]] are generally affected by the following modifiers:
*{{Ench|Looting}} (all items except pets)
*{{Ench|Luck}} (armor pieces only)

Certain other sources, such as the [[RNG Meter]] for slayers, {{Item|Hound Pet}}, or {{Item|Mole Pet}} can also increase the base drop chance of certain items.

Most items with drop chances that are lower than {{Green|5%}} after the above modifications are generally affected by {{stat|Magic Find}} (as well as {{stat|Pet Luck}} if it is a pet).

A general formula is as follows (with non-applicable buffs being set to 0):

<math>\text{Base Chance} \times \left(1 + \text{Looting Level} \times 0.15 \right) \times \left(1 + \text{Luck Level} \times 0.05\right) \times \left(1 + \frac{\text{Magic Find + Pet Luck}}{100}\right)</math>

For drops from [[Pests]], {{Ench|Looting}} and {{Ench|Luck}} do not apply even if the player swaps to a weapon with those enchantments. Additionally, instead of {{stat|Magic Find}}, {{stat|Overbloom}} is used. The formula looks like this:

<math>\text{Base Chance} \times \left(1 + \frac{\text{Overbloom}}{100}\right)</math>

Note that guaranteed drops from Pests use {{stat|Farming Fortune}} and {{stat|Crop Fortune}} with a different scaling formula.

